## Directive edge cases

Mid-line fence mention (must stay plain text — no directive opens):

Use ```{note} to create a note in MyST.

Code directives with languages:

```{code-block} python
def fenced():
    pass
```

```{code} javascript
const a = 1;
```

```{code-block} bash
echo hi
```

Colon directives with languages:

:::python
def colon_directive():
    pass
:::

:::{code-block} bash
echo colon bash
:::

Unknown language colon fence (no fold region may open):

:::kotlin
val x = 1
:::

Nested fence lengths (inner 3-fence must not close outer 4-fence):

````{note}
Outer directive (4 backticks).

```{code}
inner example
```
````

4-fence code directive with a language (inner 3-fence must not close it):

````{code-block} python
def nested_code_directive():
    pass

```{code}
inner example
```
````

Nested colon fences:

::::{important}
Outer directive (4 colons).

:::{note}
Inner directive (3 colons).
:::
::::

Option keys with no space in the key:

```{code-block} python
---
linenos: true
---
x = 1
```

## Roles

Here is {ref}`a simple role`.

Here is {ref}`Explicit text <#heading>`.

Domain role: {py:class}`MyClass`.

Math role: {math}`a < b` (edge case: < not a target).

Autolink: <path:example.txt>

Intersphinx autolink: <inv:sphinx:std#index>

## Math

Inline math: $E = mc^2$ and more text.

Escaped dollars: \$E = mc^2\$ should not be math.

$$
y = ax^2 + bx + c
$$

$$ e = mc^2 $$ (eqn:einstein)

\begin{gather*}
a_1 = b_1 + c_1 \\
a_2 = b_2 + c_2
\end{gather*}

\begin{align}
f(x) &= x^2 \\
g(x) &= x^3
\end{align}

