## Markdown parity checks

Task list:

- [x] Finish my changes
- [ ] Push my commits

Bare URL as normal text: http://example.com

Intentional line break via two trailing spaces  
and this text continues on the next line.

Emoji and highlight: :joy: :+1: ==very important words==

Titled inline link: [an example](http://example.com/ "Title")

Reference target with title:

[id2]: http://example.com/  "Optional Title Here"

Image inside a link: [![Alt text](https://url/to/img.svg)](https://link.com/)

> block quote _italic_
> more block quote

- list item followed by a blockquote

  > quoted inside a list item

Code spans of varying run length: `simple`, ``simple ` ``, ```a `` b```, and ``a`b``.

Line ending with a closed code span: see `pkg`

Escaped pipe inside a table:

| Col   | Note   |
| ----- | ------ |
| a     | \| this |

Inline HTML: &copy; <strong>bold</strong> <code>code</code> <!-- a comment -->

<table>
    <tr>
        <th>a</th>
        <th>b</th>
    </tr>
</table>

Title: some text

Italic and bold combos: ***ib*** __b__ **_ib_** ___ib___

Escapes within emphasis: \*normal text* and _text\_ more_

Tilde fence:

~~~bash
echo "$f"
~~~

